  "reproduced": [
    "Native strong spans on unindented list/quote continuations begin two or four bytes too far right",
    "Partially consumed tabs leave synthetic spaces in native inline buffers, shifting Unicode highlighting",
    "Recursive dialect contexts reuse their initial column base on later lines",
    "Multiline native HTML endpoints omit the final tag byte"
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Generic opt-in cmark inline-context enter/exit observers; first-party mapping policy is Swift",
    "Byte-identity-verified physical-line maps preserve native grammar, source bytes, literals and ownership",
    "A partially consumed tab maps its synthetic leading spaces to the one original tab byte",
    "Recursive contexts derive their map from the exact outer buffer slice; each descendant is mapped once",
    "Native multiline endpoints now retain the context base; HTML counts the complete already-recognized lexeme",
    "Only context-scoped pointers are borrowed; root completion clears recursive-context identities",
    "Finalized single-line blocks avoid redundant scanning; already-correct positions avoid redundant descendant traversal"
